From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Varun Gupta <varun.gupta1@intel.com>
Date: Mon, 27 Apr 2026 09:00:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] trace: Guard newly added xe_exec_queue trace events for older
 assign_str

The kernel grew two more TP_fast_assign() blocks in xe_trace.h:
xe_exec_queue_multi_queue (DECLARE_EVENT_CLASS) and the
xe_exec_queue_reach_max_job_count event. Both use the single-argument
form of __assign_str() introduced in v6.10 (see 2c92ca849fcc
"tracing/treewide: Remove second parameter of __assign_str()").

Older kernels still expect the two-argument form, so wrap these new
sites in BPM_ASSIGN_STR_SECOND_ARG_PRESENT just like the existing
xe_exec_queue/xe_gt_tlb_invalidation_fence entries.

Reference-id: 2c92ca849fcc tracing/treewide: Remove second parameter of __assign_str()

Signed-off-by: Varun Gupta <varun.gupta1@intel.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_trace.h | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_trace.h b/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_trace.h
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_trace.h
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_trace.h
@@ -123,7 +123,11 @@ DECLARE_EVENT_CLASS(xe_exec_queue_multi_queue,
 			     ),
 
 		    TP_fast_assign(
+#ifdef BPM_ASSIGN_STR_SECOND_ARG_PRESENT
+			   __assign_str(dev, __dev_name_eq(q));
+#else
 			   __assign_str(dev);
+#endif
 			   __entry->class = q->class;
 			   __entry->logical_mask = q->logical_mask;
 			   __entry->gt_id = q->gt->info.id;
@@ -521,7 +525,11 @@ TRACE_EVENT(xe_exec_queue_reach_max_job_count,
 			     __field(int, max_cnt)
 			     ),
 
+#ifdef BPM_ASSIGN_STR_SECOND_ARG_PRESENT
+	    TP_fast_assign(__assign_str(dev, __dev_name_eq(q));
+#else
 	    TP_fast_assign(__assign_str(dev);
+#endif
 			   __entry->class = q->class;
 			   __entry->logical_mask = q->logical_mask;
 			   __entry->guc_id = q->guc->id;
-- 
2.43.0

